# Premium layout and 3D / motion excellence

Visual work in this project should aim for a **clean, sleek, modern, carefully designed** result—never generic, never cluttered.

## Layout and composition

- Strong grid, alignment, and spacing rhythm; every section should feel **intentionally composed**
- Clear hierarchy: what to read first, second, and third
- Generous whitespace where it supports clarity; avoid cramped or arbitrary gaps
- Depth (layers, glass, gradients) only when it **sharpens** the premium feel, not to decorate randomly
- Keep layouts **consistent** with the rest of the site unless a section is deliberately asymmetric

## 3D, canvas, and immersive motion

The stack may include **Three.js**, **PixiJS**, **Theatre.js**, and related canvas work (see project README and `src/canvas/`). When adding or refining 3D / WebGL / canvas:

- Use it to **support the narrative** (hero, key moments, subtle depth)—not as a gimmick
- Prefer **refined, restrained** motion: smooth camera or object motion, tasteful lighting, readable framing
- Respect **performance**: lazy-load heavy canvas where the project already does; avoid unnecessary always-on loops
- Honor **`prefers-reduced-motion`**: provide simpler or static fallbacks when motion is reduced
- Integrate with **GSAP / Locomotive** so scroll and 3D feel like **one system**, not competing effects
- Do not rip out existing canvas or animation architecture; **extend and refine** (see `preserve-existing-work.mdc`)

## Overall bar

- **Best design** here means: polished, intentional, agency-grade—aligned with Poppr-inspired premium presentation and healthcare credibility (`project-context.mdc`, `design-direction.mdc`)
- **Sleek** means: clear structure, controlled color, no visual noise
- **Carefully designed** means: decisions are visible in spacing, type scale, and motion timing—not accidental

See also `design-direction.mdc`, `responsive-mobile-first.mdc`, and `preserve-existing-work.mdc`.
